[00:05.000 – 00:10.000] {S1} sets his chopsticks down, looks across at her and says it plainly, with the first unguarded expression he has worn all film: <d>[Chinese] 这顿饭，比相亲重要。</d> She meets his eyes and lets out a small, real laugh.
[00:10.000 – 00:15.000] She reaches across and takes one more rib from the plate, drops it into the boy's bowl off-frame, and settles back. The camera pulls back slowly on the lit table — three places, one pot, no performance left in the room. Hold and settle.

overall_soundscape:
A quiet home at night, cutlery on ceramic, a chair shifting, a child's satisfied noise off-frame, warm room tone. Two short lines of Chinese dialogue and a laugh.

non_diegetic_music:
The theme in full, warm and unadorned, resolving and fading to nothing.""",
